                <pb facs="0068" n="58" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv05/pg58"/>

                <head>Appendix III</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Draft No. 1</hi></p>
                <p>Nothing contained in or omitted from, the foregoing schedule shall restrict the
                    restoration of Belgium contemplated by point 7 of the address of the President
                    of the United States to Congress, made January 7 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >8</hi>], 1918, and concurred in by the Allied and Associated Governments.</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Draft No. 2</hi></p>
                <p>Nothing contained in, or omitted from, the foregoing schedule shall operate to
                    limit the making of such reparation for that damage done to Belgium as will
                    serve to restore confidence among the nations in the laws which they have
                    themselves set and determined for the Government of their relations with one
                    another, and without which the whole structure and validity of international law
                    is forever impaired.</p>
            </div>
